<p>Some key concepts related to decimal fractions include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Place value</strong>: The value of a digit depending on its position in a number. For example, in the number 0.5, the 5 is in the tenths place.</li>
<li><strong>Rounding</strong>: The process of approximating a number to a certain place value. For example, 0.55 can be rounded to 0.6.</li>
<li><strong>Comparing decimal fractions</strong>: The process of determining which of two decimal fractions is larger or smaller. For example, 0.5 is less than 0.6.</li>
